  "articleBody": "Even with careful planning, sometimes pull-out cabinet shelves can present a few hiccups. It's usually something solvable! If your shelf isn't extending or retracting smoothly, first check if the slides are level. Uneven mounting is a common culprit. Grab a level and adjust as needed. Another issue could be choosing the wrong width or depth for your shelf, leading to it catching or not fully extending. Double-check your initial measurements against the shelf size. Sometimes, existing hinges or the cabinet's face frame can obstruct the shelf's movement; you might need different hardware or to adjust the mounting position. Lastly, make sure you haven't overloaded the shelf beyond its weight capacity. This can cause the slides to bind or even damage the hardware. If you're dealing with complex issues like hidden plumbing, uneven framing, or if multiple shelves need consistent alignment, don't hesitate to reach out to a professional. HH Remodeling LLC can handle these tricky installations, ensuring everything works perfectly in your Denver home.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}